course: dictionary
lesson: 14790
title: Publisher: who makes books and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A publisher is a company or person that prepares books, magazines, newspapers, music or games and makes them available for people to buy or read. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it. «The publisher printed a thousand copies of the new book.» Printing copies and selling them tells you what a publisher does.
explain: Here is a second meaning, from computers. «The school used a publisher to put our class project online for families to see.» Putting something online for others to see is the clue, so this publisher is a program or person that shares work on the internet.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The company that prepares the book printed a thousand copies» still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right. If it does not fit, read on and look for more clues, or check a dictionary.
fact: A publisher is a company or person that prepares books, magazines, newspapers, music or games.
fact: «A children's publisher» means a publisher that makes books for young readers.
fact: «Find a publisher» means to find a company that might print and sell your book.
fact: The publisher's name is usually on a book's spine and title page.
fact: On a computer, a publisher can be a program or person that puts something online for others to see.
exercise: «The publisher printed a thousand copies of the new book.» What is a publisher? | A machine that folds paper | A shop that only sells pencils | *A company that prepares and sells books | A person who reads books aloud in a library
exercise: Mia wants to «find a publisher» for her story. What does this mean? | To buy a new pen | *To find a company that might print and sell her story | To write a story about a publisher | To find a lost book in the library
exercise: «The school used a publisher to put our class project online.» In this sentence, what does publisher mean? | A teacher who marks books | A person who sells cakes | A company that makes music only | *A program or person that puts something online
test: «Her children's publisher only makes books for young readers.» What does children's publisher mean? | A teacher of reading | A library for grown-ups | *A company that makes books for children | A child who writes books
test: Which of these can a publisher prepare and make available? | *A newspaper | A lamp | A puddle | A chair
exam: «The publisher's name is printed on the title page of the book.» Where would you usually find the publisher's name? | On the bus | Under the bed | *On the title page | In the sky
